This file is not a licence and does not become one by sitting where a licence
usually sits. It says that there is none.

## Why the dual licence is gone

From M0 until 14.08.2026 this repository declared `MIT OR Apache-2.0`, in two
files here and in the `license` field of every manifest. Both of those grants
are irrevocable for any copy published under them, and the direction this
project has since been given for its licensing is incompatible with them (D5,
reopened 11.08.2026). **The old grant was removed while the source was still
unpublished, and that timing is the whole of why it could be removed at all** —
a grant cannot be withdrawn from a copy somebody already holds under it.

Publication changes nothing about this. What is published is what this file
says: source that is readable, and no permission to use, copy, modify or
distribute it. The point of the removal was never that nobody could see the
code; it was that nobody had been given terms.

Removing the old licence is deliberately **not** a choice of a new one. What
Narvo will be licensed under is open, it is a human's decision, and D5 records
that it is taken with legal advice before any release. Nothing here anticipates
it.

## What this file does not cover

Third-party material keeps its own terms, which are its authors' to give and
not ours to withdraw. That includes every dependency in `Cargo.lock` and the
DejaVu Sans Mono font under `crates/narvo-testkit/assets/`, whose own licence
sits beside it because its terms require it to travel with the font.
